---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { contactEmail, updated, refundDays, price } from "../legal";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const h2 = "prose-h2";
const p = "prose-p";
const ul = "prose-ul";
const link = "prose-a";
---

<Layout
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy — Minnie"
  description="Thirty days, no reason needed. How to cancel, how to get your money back, and what happens to Minnie afterwards."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="legal">
    <a href={base} class="legal__back mono">← back to home</a>

    <h1 class="legal__h1">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__date mono">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class={p} style="margin-top:28px;">
      Minnie has a free trial precisely so you can find out whether she fits before
      paying. If you paid anyway and she does not, we would rather give the money back
      than keep it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Refunds</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      <strong>Within {refundDays} days of a charge, you can have a full refund, and
      you do not have to give a reason.</strong> Email <a class={link} href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> from the address you
      bought with, and we will process it.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Refunds go back to the original payment method. Once processed on our side, your
      bank usually takes another 5–10 working days to show it — that part is not
      something we can speed up.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      After {refundDays} days we do not refund a period already under way, but you can
      cancel at any time so it does not renew. If something has gone genuinely wrong —
      a double charge, a subscription you cancelled that billed anyway, a build that
      never worked on your Mac — write to us regardless of the date. Those are
      mistakes, not refund requests, and we fix them.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Cancelling</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Open <strong>Settings ▸ Account ▸ Manage subscription</strong> in Minnie, which
      takes you to the customer portal for the email you bought with. You can also
      just email us and we will cancel it for you.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Cancelling stops the next renewal. <strong>It does not cut you off
      immediately</strong> — you keep full access until the end of the period you have
      already paid for. You paid for the year; you get the year.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What happens after</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie does not disappear and does not lock your work away. When the paid period
      ends she stops running agent tasks, but she still appears, listens and speaks,
      and everything on your Mac — her memory of you, your task history, your settings
      — stays exactly where it is. Subscribe again later and she picks up where she
      left off.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Failed payments</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      A declined card is usually a bank being cautious, not a decision. If a renewal
      fails we keep your access on and give the payment a grace period to go through
      before anything changes. We do not lock you out the same day.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Trials</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The trial needs no card, so it cannot charge you and there is nothing to cancel.
      When it ends, it ends — you are not billed unless you choose to subscribe.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Price</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Minnie is {price}. Any discount you used applies for as long as your
      subscription stays active.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Chargebacks</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Please email us before raising a chargeback. A bank dispute takes months and
      locks the account while it runs; we can usually refund you the same day. We have
      never refused a request made in good faith.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      <a class={link} href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Include the
      email you paid with and we will find the rest.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      See also the <a class={link} href={`${base}terms`}>Terms of Service</a> and the <a class={link} href={`${base}privacy`}>Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
